# pnpm settings for this package.
#
# The pnpm store is machine state, not repository state: pnpm resolves it from
# its own configuration (on this machine `D:\.pnpm-store`). Pinning `store-dir`
# here would point pnpm at a second, duplicate store rather than reuse the
# existing one, and setting it to a relative path does not reliably apply —
# `pnpm config get store-dir` still reports the global location. Reproducibility
# therefore rests on `pnpm-lock.yaml`, which pins every dependency to an exact
# version and integrity hash; a fresh checkout needs only `pnpm install` with
# the lockfile present.
#
# The virtual store stays at its default, `node_modules/.pnpm`, so the linked
# tree is local to this package and is removed with `node_modules/`.
#
# Install from a normal shell rather than inside a DSH session: pnpm creates its
# store-operation lock next to the store, outside the workspace, which DSH's
# `workspace-write` sandbox refuses.
